ng him from gold medal contention. That left the event wide open and allowed Ukrainian " [:a {:href "/athletes/60427"} "V’iacheslav Oliynyk"] " to advance to the final, after he defeated Başar in the semi-finals. Oliynyk was the 1994 European Champion and had been runner-up at the 1994 Worlds, but was 30-years-old in 1996 and even his wife considered him too old to contend for medals. In the final he met " [:a {:href "/athletes/59628"} "Jacek Fafiński"] " of Poland, who had finished eighth at the recent Europeans and in his career, would stand on one international podium – this one. Oliynyk had no difficulty winning the gold medal, defeating Fafiński 6-0 in the final."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60427"} "V'iacheslav Oliynyk"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UKR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UKR.png"}] "UKR"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59628"} "Jacek Fafiński"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "13"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58337"} "Maik Bullmann"]]